messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA certain meeting invited six people from a certain workplace: Zhang, Wang, Li, Zhao, Sun, and Zhou to attend. However, due to work arrangements, all six people cannot go to the meeting at the same time. Among them: Only one person between Zhang and Zhao can attend the meeting; Also Only one person between Li and Zhao can attend the meeting; At least one person between Zhang and Wang can attend the meeting; Two of the three among Zhang, Sun, and Zhou can attend the meeting; Wang and Li either both attend the meeting or neither of them attend the meeting; if Zhao will not attend the meeting, then Sun will not attend the meeting either.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to this arrangement, Which one probably will not attend the meeting in the end?\n# Options:\nA) Zhang and wang\nB) Wang and li\nC) Li and zhao\nD) Zhao and sun', "<think>.\nTo solve this problem, let's analyze the given information step by step:.\n\n1.**Only one person between Zhang and Zhao can attend the meeting**: This means either Zhang or Zhao will attend, but not both.\n2.**Only one person between Li and Zhao can attend the meeting**: This means either Li or Zhao will attend, but not both.\n3.**At least one person between Zhang and Wang can attend the meeting**: This means either Zhang or Wang will attend, but not both.\n4.**Two of the three among Zhang, Sun, and Zhou can attend the meeting**: This means exactly two of these three individuals will attend.\n5.**Wang and Li either both attend the meeting or neither of them attend the meeting**: This means if Wang attends, then Li also attends, and vice versa.\n6.**If Zhao will not attend the meeting, then Sun will not attend the meeting either**: This means if Zhao does not attend, then Sun also does not attend.\n\nNow, let's consider the possible combinations based on these rules:.\n\n- Since both Zhang and Zhao can attend, we have two scenarios: Zhang attends and Zhao does not, or Zhao attends and Zhang does not.\n- Since both Li and Zhao can attend, we have two scenarios: Li attends and Zhao does not, or Zhao attends and Li does not.\n- Since both Zhang and Wang can attend, we have two scenarios: Zhang attends and Wang does not, or Wang attends and Zhang does not.\n- Since all three among Zhang, Sun, and Zhou can attend, we have three scenarios: Zhang and Sun attend, Zhang and Zhou attend, or Sun and Zhou attend.\n- Since Wang and Li either both attend or neither of them attend, we need to consider these two cases together.\n- If Zhao does not attend, then Sun also does not attend.\n\nLet's evaluate each option:\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
