of Tiktaalik could not be determined just through comparison to fish species of its time.\n- This statement is supported by the information given.Since variations were great among prehistoric fish species, Tiktaalik would not have stood out as unusual at the time.Therefore, the evolutionary significance of Tiktaalik could not be determined just through comparison to fish species of its time.This option is correct.\n\nThere is no doubt that fish without fingers can easily move on land, contrary to the claim made. Tiktaalik's fingers were significant in animal evolution, but it's wrong to say that no fish without fingers can move on land. This option is accurate and supported by the information given.\n\nAccording to the analysis, the correct answer is B) The evolutionary importance of Tiktaalik can be clearly understood by comparing it to other fish species of its time.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
