messages:   13%|#3        | 78/600 [02:53<03:49,  2.27it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nCollege student Xiao Wang took the Postgraduate Admission Test exam in four subjects: politics, English, major one, major two. The sum of the scores of political and professional subject one is equal to the sum of the scores of the other two subjects.The sum of the scores of the political and professional subjects two is greater than the sum of the scores of the other two subjects. The scores of the professional subject one are higher than the sum of the scores of the political and English subjects.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above conditions, which of the following is the correct ranking of Xiao Wang's four subjects from high to low?\n# Options:\nA) Major subject one, major subject two, english, politics.\nB) Major subject two, major subject one, politics, english.\nC) Major subject one, major subject two, politics, english.\nD) Major subject two, major subject one, english, politics.", "<think>.\nTo determine the correct ranking of Xiao Wang's four subjects from high to low, let's analyze the given information step by step:.\n\n1.**Sum of Political and Professional Subject One**: This sum is equal to the sum of the scores of the other two subjects (English and Major Two).Let's denote the scores as follows:.\n   - Political: P.\n   - English: E.\n   - Major One: M1.\n   - Major Two: M2.\n\n   So, we have:.\n   P + M1 = E + M2.\n\n2.**Sum of Political and Professional Subject Two**: This sum is greater than the sum of the scores of the other two subjects (English and Major One).So, we have:.\n   P + M2 > E + M1.\n\n3.**Scores of Major Subject One**: The scores of Major Subject One are higher than the sum of the scores of Political and English subjects.So, we have:.\n   M1 > P + E.\n\nNow, let's analyze the options based on these conditions:.\n\nA) Major subject one, major subject two, english, politics.\n   - This option suggests that Major Subject One is higher than English, which contradicts the third condition (M1 > P + E).\n\nB) Major subject two, major subject one, politics, english.\n   - This option suggests that Major Subject Two is higher than Major Subject One, which contradicts the first condition (P + M1 = E + M2).\n\nC) Major subject one, major subject two, politics, english.\n   - This option suggests that Major Subject One is higher than Major Subject Two, which contradicts the first condition (P + M1 = E + M2).Your output. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
