messages:   22%|##2       | 132/600 [05:24<02:23,  3.26it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNations that have little interaction with one another have little knowledge of one another' s needs and problems. Because both sympathy and justice depend largely on understanding the needs and problems of others, it follows that__.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following most logically completes the argument?\n# Options:\nA) Only nations that have some interaction with one another have knowledge of one another's needs and problems\nB) Without some interaction, nations are bound to find it difficult to extend sympathy and justice to one another\nC) There is no way to eliminate conflict among nations\nD) Almost all problems between nations stem from lack of sympathy and justice", "<think>.\nTo determine the correct answer, let's analyze the given context and question step by step:.\n\n1.The context states that nations with little interaction have limited knowledge of each other's needs and problems.\n2.Sympathy and justice depend on understanding the needs and problems of others.\n3.Therefore, it follows that nations with little interaction will have difficulty extending sympathy and justice to one another.\n\nNow, let's examine the options:.\n\nA) Only nations that have some interaction with one another have knowledge of one another's needs and problems.\nThis option contradicts the context, which states that nations with little interaction have limited knowledge of each other's needs and problems.\n\nB) Without some interaction, nations are bound to find it difficult to extend sympathy and justice to one another.\nThis option aligns with the context, as it states that nations with little interaction will have difficulty extending sympathy and justice to one another.\nWithout any interaction, nations will easily be able to extend sympathy and justice to one another.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
