messages:   32%|###1      | 190/600 [07:53<01:35,  4.31it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn the process of accompanying their children, many parents will encounter the problem of their children lying or concealing the truth. Lying is almost what many parents are most worried about. Their children's bad behavior is even more frightening and angry than their children's poor academic performance.If we say that many parents have not solved the problem of their children lying well, at least most of them should pay attention to it, while the problem of children concealing their own situation from their parents is not only worse solved, but also not given enough attention.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is true of the original text?\n# Options:\nA) Parents think that children's failure to report information is more worrying than lying\nB) Parents believe that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem\nC) Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying\nD) Children's behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents", '<think>.\nTo determine which option is true based on the given context, let\'s analyze each statement step by step:.\n\n1.**Statement A**: "Parents think that children\'s failure to report information is more worrying than lying.".\n   - The context mentions that "many parents will encounter the problem of their children lying or concealing the truth," but it does not specifically state that parents worry more about children failing to report information than lying.Therefore, this statement cannot be confirmed as true based on the given information.\n\n2.**Statement B**: "Parents believe that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem.".\n   - The context does not provide any information about parents\' beliefs regarding the severity of lying compared to other moral problems.Thus, we cannot conclude that this statement is true based on the given information.\n\n3.**Statement C**: "Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying.Statement D: "Parents have been very observant and concerned about their children concealing their own situation.".\n- The context clearly indicates that parents are highly attentive and worried about their children concealing their own situation, which goes against the idea that parents have not paid attention to this behavior. Therefore, this statement can be considered true based on the provided information.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
