messages:   35%|###4      | 208/600 [08:00<01:52,  3.47it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nDirect selling refers to the business mode in which direct selling enterprises recruit sellers to sell products directly to final consumers outside the fixed business place.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is direct selling?\n# Options:\nA) After selecting salesmen, a dairy manufacturer set up 100 sales points in the city to sell dairy products at a unified price.\nB) A bookstore adopts online sales. after customers place an order, the courier will send the products to the designated place and charge a fee.\nC) Some salesmen recruited by a cosmetics brand set up stalls along the road to distribute product descriptions and sell them to customers at lower prices.\nD) At the beginning of school, the new student xiao he bought five table lamps in the wholesale market, one for his own use, and the other four were sold to his classmates.', "<think>.\nTo determine which option represents direct selling, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) After selecting salesmen, a dairy manufacturer set up 100 sales points in the city to sell dairy products at a unified price.\n- This option describes a scenario where the manufacturer sets up sales points to sell its products.However, it does not involve direct selling because the salesmen are not selling the products directly to final consumers outside the fixed business place.Instead, they are selling to customers within the city, which is not considered direct selling.\n\nB) A bookstore adopts online sales.After customers place an order, the courier will send the products to the designated place and charge a fee.\n- This option describes an online sales model where customers place orders and the products are delivered to them.While this is a form of indirect selling, it is not direct selling because the products are not being sold directly to the customers outside the bookstore's fixed business place.\n\nC) Some salesmen recruited by a cosmetics brand set up stalls along the road to distribute product descriptions and sell them to customers at lower prices.\n- This option describes a scenario where salesmen are setting up stalls to sell products directly to customers outside the fixed business place.This is a clear example of direct selling because the salesmen are selling the products directly to the customers.At the beginning of school, the new student xiao he bought five table lamps in the wholesale market, one for his own use, and the other four were sold to his classmates. This scenario involves a student purchasing items for personal use and then distributing them to classmates for free. The student is not engaged in any selling activities to make a profit.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
