messages:   37%|###6      | 220/600 [08:03<01:14,  5.11it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe star-nosed mole has a nose that ends in a pair of several-pointed stars, or tentacles that are crucial for hunting, as moles are poor-sighted. These tentacles contain receptors that detect electric fields produced by other animals, enabling the moles to detect and catch suitable prey such as worms and insects.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following is most strongly supported by the information above?\n# Options:\nA) Both worms and insects produce electric fields.\nB) Only animals that hunt have noses with tentacles that detect electric fields.\nC) The star-nosed mole does not produce an electric field.\nD) The star-nosed mole does not rely at all on its sense of smell when hunting.', "<think>.\nTo determine which option is most strongly supported by the given information, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) Both worms and insects produce electric fields.\nThe context does not mention that only animals that hunt have noses with tentacles that detect electric fields; therefore, we can conclude that both worms and insects produce electric fields based on the given information.\n\nD) Only animals that do not hunt have noses with tentacles that detect electric fields\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
