messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nInvisible curriculum refers to the informal and unconscious learning experience that is not clearly specified in the school's planned curriculum.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is not an invisible curriculum?\n# Options:\nA) Colleges and universities organize students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students' willpower.\nB) When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching.\nC) A university set up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study.\nD) Teachers and students participate in extracurricular activities together to establish an equal and harmonious relationship between teachers and students.", "<think>.\nTo determine which option is not an example of an invisible curriculum, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) Colleges and universities organizing students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students' willpower - This is an example of an invisible curriculum because it is an informal and unconscious learning experience that is not clearly specified in the school's planned curriculum.It is a way to develop character and discipline among students.\n\nB) When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching - This is also an example of an invisible curriculum because it is an informal and unconscious learning experience that is not clearly specified in the school's planned curriculum.It is a way to develop a passion for teaching among students.\n\nC) A university setting up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study - This is an example of an invisible curriculum because it is an informal and unconscious learning experience that is not clearly specified in the school's planned curriculum.It is a way to promote the school's values and culture among students.\n\nEngaging in extracurricular activities with teachers is a clear example of an invisible curriculum, as it fosters an equal and harmonious relationship between teachers and students, and is not a structured part of the school's planned curriculum. It helps to maintain a positive bond between teachers and students.\n\nAfter careful consideration, the appropriate choice is A) Teachers and students engaging in extracurricular activities to create a hierarchical and distant relationship between teachers and students.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
