messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSmithtown University' s fund-raisers succeeded in getting donations from 80 percent of the potential donors they contacted. This success rate, exceptionally high for university fund-raisers, does not indicate that they were doing a good job. On the contrary, since the people most likely to donate are those who have donated in the past, good fund-raisers constantly try less-likely prospects in an effort to expand the donor base. The high success rate shows insufficient canvassing effort.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, provides more support for the argument?\n# Options:\nA) This year the average size of the donations to smithtown university from new donors when the university's fund-raisers had contacted was larger than the average size of donations from donors who had given to the university before.\nB) The majority of the donations that fund-raisers succeeded in getting for smithtown university this year were from donors who had never given to the university before.\nC) This year most of the donations that came to smithtown university from people who had previously donated to it were made without the university's fund-raisers having made any contact with the donors.\nD) Smithtown university's fund-raisers were successful in their contacts with potential donors who had never given before about as frequently as were fund-raisers for other universities in their contacts with such people.", "<think>.\nTo determine which option provides more support for the argument, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) This year the average size of the donations to Smithtown University from new donors when the university's fund-raisers had contacted was larger than the average size of donations from donors who had given to the university before.\nThis option suggests that the high success rate may be due to the fact that the fund-raisers were able to secure larger donations from new donors rather than from existing donors.This could potentially undermine the argument that the high success rate indicates insufficient canvassing effort.\n\nB) The majority of the donations that fund-raisers succeeded in getting for Smithtown University this year were from donors who had never given to the university before.\nThis option directly supports the argument that the high success rate is due to the fund-raisers' efforts to contact less-likely prospects.If the majority of the donations came from new donors, it suggests that the fund-raisers were indeed making an effort to expand the donor base.\n\nC) This year most of the donations that came to Smithtown University from people who had previously donated to it were made without the university's fund-raisers having made any contact with the donors.\nThis option contradicts the argument that the high success rate indicates insufficient canvassing effort.If most of the donations came from donors who had previously given without the fund-raisers' contact, it suggests that the fund-raisers were not making an effort to contact these donors.The success rate of Smithtown university's fund-raisers in contacting potential donors who had never given before was not as frequent as fund-raisers for other universities in their contacts with such people.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
