ception of accomplished non-native speakers.Therefore, this option is not an assumption on which the argument depends.\n\nC) It is impossible to understand sentences if they are in fact uninterrupted streams of sound.\n- This option suggests that it is impossible to understand sentences if they are in fact uninterrupted streams of sound.However, the argument does not make any claims about the impossibility of understanding sentences.Therefore, this option is not an assumption on which the argument depends.\nPeople pay more attention to the way their own language sounds than they do to the way an unfamiliar language sounds.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
