quantity of food they consume. The information available in the context confirms the strong correlation between the number of meals and the amount of food ingested. Therefore, Option C is well-supported.\n\nOption D: This option proposes that the quantity of food individuals consume is not significantly impacted by the timing of their meals. The context clearly indicates a lack of evidence regarding the connection between eating time and food intake. Hence, Option D is well-supported.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
