messages:   48%|####7     | 285/600 [13:01<00:57,  5.48it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nBroken window effect is a psychological phenomenon, that is, if the window of a house is broken and no one repair it, and soon other windows will also be broken.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which one of the followings does not belong to broken window effect?\n# Options:\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\nD) If a few people in a group speak uncivilized languages and are not stopped, many people will soon speak uncivilized languages.', "<think>.\nTo determine which option does not belong to the broken window effect, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\n- This option describes a situation where one person's action (not cleaning graffiti) leads to a chain reaction (other people also leaving graffiti).This aligns with the broken window effect, as it shows how one person's inaction can lead to a deterioration of the environment.\n\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\n- This option describes a situation where one source of pollution (a tributary) can affect the entire basin.This aligns with the broken window effect, as it shows how one source of pollution can lead to a deterioration of the environment.\n\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\n- This option describes a situation where one person's action (throwing rubbish) leads to a chain reaction (other people also throwing rubbish).This aligns with the broken window effect, as it shows how one person's inaction can lead to a deterioration of the environment.If a few people in a group speak civilized languages and are stopped, many people will soon speak civilized languages.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
