messages:   50%|####9     | 298/600 [13:05<01:06,  4.51it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOrthodox medicine is ineffective at both ends of the spectrum of ailments. At the more trivial end, orthodox medicine is largely ineffective in treating aches, pains, and allergies, and, at the other extreme, it has yet to produce a cure for serious, life-threatening diseases such as advanced cancer and lupus. People turn to alternative medicine when orthodox medicine fails to help them and when it produces side effects that are unacceptable to them. One of the reasons alternative medicine is free of such side effects is that it does not have any effects at all.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if the statements above are true, which one of the following can be properly inferred from them?\n# Options:\nA) Orthodox medicine will eventually produce a solution for the diseases that are currently incurable.\nB) There are some medical conditions for which no orthodox or alternative treatment is effective.\nC) There are some trivial illnesses that can be treated effectively by the methods of alternative medicine.\nD) Practitioners of alternative medicine are acting in bad faith.', "<think>.\nTo determine which option can be properly inferred from the given context, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) Orthodox medicine will eventually produce a solution for the diseases that are currently incurable.\n- The context states that orthodox medicine has yet to produce a cure for serious, life-threatening diseases like advanced cancer and lupus.This implies that orthodox medicine may not be able to produce a solution for these incurable diseases in the future.Therefore, option A cannot be properly inferred.\n\nB) There are some medical conditions for which no orthodox or alternative treatment is effective.\n- The context mentions that people turn to alternative medicine when orthodox medicine fails to help them and produces side effects they find unacceptable.This suggests that there are indeed medical conditions for which neither orthodox nor alternative treatments are effective.Therefore, option B can be properly inferred.\n\nC) There are some trivial illnesses that can be treated effectively by the methods of alternative medicine.\n- The context states that alternative medicine is free of side effects and does not have any effects at all.This implies that alternative medicine may be effective in treating trivial illnesses without causing any side effects.Therefore, option C can be properly inferred.\nPractitioners of alternative medicine are acting in good faith.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
