messages:   56%|#####6    | 336/600 [13:17<00:57,  4.63it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn recent years, community banks in some big cities have been closed frequently. At the same time, a series of new banks, such as unmanned banks, 5G banks and smart banks, keep emerging. Bank branches are bidding farewell to cold glass counters and metal benches. The traditional transaction processing functions of bank branches are weakened, and customized services, product experience, social interaction and other functions are increasingly prominent. As a result, some experts predict that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings, if true, best supports the expert's view?\n# Options:\nA) Customers need to enter the door to take the number, wait for the number, to deal with a simple business cost a long time\nB) The introduction of artificial intelligence and other technological means has changed people's impression of bank branches\nC) Complex business must be signed face to face at the bank branch, such as account opening, account cancellation, etc., must be handled by myself and manual audit\nD) Online banking, mobile banking and other emerging, bank outlets as the main channel of service is weakening", "<think>.\nTo determine which option best supports the expert's view that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) Customers need to enter the door to take the number, wait for the number, to deal with a simple business cost a long time - This option suggests that customers still need to visit physical branches for certain transactions, which contradicts the idea that traditional bank branches will disappear.Therefore, this option does not support the expert's view.\n\nB) The introduction of artificial intelligence and other technological means has changed people's impression of bank branches - This option indicates that technological advancements have altered how people perceive bank branches, making them more efficient and convenient.This aligns with the expert's prediction that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years.Therefore, this option supports the expert's view.\n\nC) Complex business must be signed face to face at the bank branch, such as account opening, account cancellation, etc., must be handled by myself and manual audit - This option highlights the importance of face-to-face interactions in handling complex transactions, which suggests that traditional bank branches may still be necessary for certain services.This contradicts the expert's view that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years.Therefore, this option does not support the expert's view.Online banking, mobile banking, and other emerging bank outlets are strengthening as the main channel of service, indicating a shift away from traditional bank branches. This option supports the expert's prediction that physical bank branches will become obsolete within 20 years, making it a stronger choice compared to option B.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
