messages:   66%|######5   | 393/600 [15:47<00:45,  4.57it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nLance: If experience teaches us nothing else, it teaches us that every general rule has at least one exception. Frank: What you conclude is itself a general rule. If we assume that it is true, then there is at least one general rule that has no exceptions. Ttherefore, you must withdraw your conclusion.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, frank's argument is an attempt to counter Lance's conclusion by\n# Options:\nA) Demonstrating that lance assumes the very thing he sets out to prove\nB) Establishing that experience teaches us the opposite of what lance concludes\nC) Showing that lance's conclusion involves him in a contradiction\nD) Showing that it has no implications for any real cases", "<think>.\nTo determine the correct answer, let's analyze the given context and question step by step:.\n\n1.**Understanding the Context**: The context presents a debate between Lance and Frank.Lance argues that every general rule has at least one exception, while Frank counters this by suggesting that if we assume this to be true, then there exists at least one general rule without exceptions.\n\n2.**Analyzing Frank's Argument**: Frank's argument can be broken down as follows:.\n   - He assumes that Lance's conclusion (every general rule has at least one exception) is true.\n   - Based on this assumption, he concludes that there is at least one general rule without exceptions.\nThis implies that Frank is not attempting to demonstrate that Lance's conclusion leads to a contradiction or an absurdity.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
