messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nField dependence means that external references are used as the basis for information processing, so it is difficult to get rid of the influence of environmental factors. Their attitude and self-perception are more easily influenced and disturbed by the people around them, especially the authorities, and they are good at observing words and emotions, paying attention to and remembering the social contents in verbal messages.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following belongs to field dependence?\n# Options:\nA) Have the ability to learn independently\nB) Have one's own opinion on the evaluation of others\nC) Doing things is dominated by intrinsic motivation\nD) Doing things is dominated by external motivation", "<think>.\nTo determine which option belongs to field dependence, let's analyze each option based on the given definition:.\n\n1.**Option A: Have the ability to learn independently**.\n   - This option suggests that someone can learn without relying on external references or environmental factors.This aligns with the definition of field independence, where individuals process information independently of external references.\n\n2.**Option B: Have one's own opinion on the evaluation of others**.\n   - This option implies that someone has their own perspective on how others are evaluated.While this might involve some level of personal judgment, it does not necessarily mean that they rely on external references for information processing.Therefore, this option does not directly align with field dependence.\n\n3.Option D: Doing things is dominated by internal motivation.\n   - Internal motivation refers to doing something for personal satisfaction or enjoyment rather than external rewards. This aligns with the definition of field independence, as individuals with internal motivation tend to process information independently of external factors.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
