messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nFor example, X X Group held an anniversary celebration, your mobile phone number won a grand prize of 100000 yuan. this kind of unwise fraudulent text messages on mobile phones still appear again and again even after they have been exposed by the media. Professional swindlers prefer to use shoddy fraudulent text messages rather than design more deceptive and gullible text messages, which only shows that the swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options, if true, strongly refutes the above conclusion?\n# Options:\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\nC) If a deception was useless, the swindler would have eliminated it long ago.\nD) Swindlers use such text messages to catch people who may be fooled, and they want to filter out smart people in the first place.', '<think>.\nTo determine which option strongly refutes the conclusion that professional swindlers prefer to use shoddy fraudulent text messages rather than design more deceptive and gullible text messages, we need to analyze each option carefully.\n\nOption A states that a swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.This option does not directly address the preference for shoddy text messages over more deceptive ones.It merely states a general characteristic of swindlers but does not provide any evidence against the given conclusion.\n\nOption B suggests that swindlers prefer to avoid attracting the attention of the police.While this might be true, it does not directly relate to the preference for shoddy text messages over more deceptive ones.It is possible that swindlers could still use shoddy text messages even if they avoid drawing attention to themselves.\n\nOption C suggests that swindlers constantly seek out ineffective methods and do not prioritize improving their techniques, particularly when it comes to text messages. It does not discuss the possibility of swindlers opting for more deceptive tactics over shoddy ones. Swindlers may still choose to utilize ineffective text messages even if they have the capability to create more successful ones.\n\nOption D implies that swindlers employ shoddy text messages to attract intelligent individuals and intentionally weed out those who can easily discern deception. This option directly supports the idea that swindlers prefer using subpar text messages to lure in specific targets rather than investing in more sophisticated and misleading communication. This argument contradicts the notion that professional swindlers favor crafting deceiving and convincing text messages over utilizing shoddy fraudulent ones.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
