it doesn't directly address the effectiveness of the device in locating trapped individuals.Therefore, this option does not strengthen the argument.\n\nB) Most people who have survived after being trapped in collapsed buildings were rescued within two hours of the building's collapse.\n- This option provides information about the time frame in which people were rescued, but it doesn't directly relate to the performance of the device in detecting signals from trapped individuals.Thus, this option does not strengthen the argument.\n\nThe device's ability to distinguish signals from human beings is not relevant to its effectiveness in locating trapped individuals. Therefore, this option does not provide any support for the argument.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
