messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is closest to the meaning of the above judgement?\n# Options:\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\nC) If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\nD) To accept the truth, we must reject wrong.', '<think>.\nTo determine the correct option, let\'s analyze the given context and question step by step:.\n\n1.The context states that "If you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out."This implies that if we close all the wrong doors, truth will be prevented from entering or being accessible.\n\n2.Now, let\'s examine each option to see which one aligns with the context:.\n\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\n- This option suggests that if truth is shut out, then all the wrong doors must have been closed.However, the context only states that closing all the wrong doors leads to truth being shut out, not the reverse.\n\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\n- This option states that truth cannot be shut out unless all the wrong doors are closed.Closing all the wrong doors does not lead to truth being shut out; on the contrary, it ensures that truth is embraced and welcomed with open arms.\n- This statement conveys that closing the wrong doors actually facilitates the acceptance and embrace of truth.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
