gineer's argument.\nNot all air conditioners need to be guaranteed to work properly in the area before they can be sold. This option implies that there is no requirement for ensuring the functionality of air conditioners in a specific area before selling them. It does not contradict the engineer's argument about local air quality. The option that most effectively refutes the engineer's argument is not A) In areas with good air quality, the brand's air conditioners work very well, but rather B) Air conditioners from the brand have been proven to malfunction in areas with poor air quality.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
