 after it has cooled.\n3.The plant manager concludes that adopting the new process will cost much but bring the company no profit.\n4.The supervisor agrees with the overall conclusion but disagrees with one point made by the plant manager.\n\nNow, let's examine the options:.\n\nA) Whether the new copper-smelting process releases less sulfur dioxide gas into the atmosphere than the current process - This option does not align with the supervisor's disagreement, as the supervisor agrees with the overall conclusion.\n\nB) Whether the new process should be adopted in the copper-smelting plant - This option does not align with the supervisor's disagreement, as the supervisor agrees with the overall conclusion.The supervisor agrees with the plant manager's statement about the new process being more expensive to run.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
