4.Classmate C guessed that Zhao Ming was admitted to Peking University and Sun Jie was admitted to Tsinghua University.\n5.The students' guesses were half right.\n\nNow, let's analyze the options:.\n\nA) Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie were admitted to Peking University, Tsinghua University, and Beijing Normal University respectively.\n- This option contradicts Classmate A's guess, as Zhao Ming was not admitted to Tsinghua University.\n\nB) Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie were admitted to Tsinghua University, Beijing Normal University, and Peking University respectively.\n- This option aligns with Classmate B's guess, as Qian Hong was admitted to Tsinghua University.\n\nC) Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie were not admitted to Beijing Normal University, Tsinghua University, and Peking University respectively.\n- This option aligns with Classmate C's guess, as Sun Jie was admitted to Tsinghua University.\n\nD) Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie were not admitted to Peking University, Beijing Normal University, and Tsinghua University respectively.\n- This option contradicts all of the students' guesses, as it does not match the given information.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie were not admitted to Peking University, Beijing Normal University, and Tsinghua University respectively.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
