 was their own campaign sponsor.Therefore, this option does not accurately point out a problem in the argument.\n\nB) The argument fails to explain the impact of the amount of campaign funding on the judicial supervision.\n- This option suggests that the argument does not provide information about how much campaign funding affects judicial decisions.However, the context does not mention anything about the amount of campaign funding, so this option does not accurately point out a problem in the argument.\n\nC) The argument ignores the fact that when campaign funding and judicial decisions are completely transparent, judicial supervision by the media is everywhere.\n- This option suggests that the argument overlooks the role of media supervision in cases where campaign funding and judicial decisions are transparent.However, the context does not mention anything about media supervision, so this option does not accurately point out a problem in the argument.\n\nD) The argument does not give the proportion of campaign funders among all the parties involved.All of the options accurately point out a problem in the given argument.\n\nNone of the options accurately point out a problem in the given argument.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
