ption aligns with the context, which states that eating too much MSG can lead to various harmful effects.\n\nB) MSG may cause cancer or other visceral diseases - This option also aligns with the context, which mentions that eating too much MSG can lead to cancer or other visceral diseases.\n\nC) Monosodium glutamate can improve people's food and martial arts, and has a certain tonic effect on the human body - This option contradicts the context, which states that MSG can enhance people's appetite, improve the human body's ability to absorb other things, and have a certain tonic effect on the human body.\nMonosodium glutamate is not harmful and can be consumed safely - This option aligns with the understanding that MSG is generally considered safe to eat in moderate amounts.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is:.\n\nC) MSG does not pose significant health risks when consumed in moderation.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
