messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nUniversity administrator: Any proposal for a new department will not be funded if there are fewer than 50 people per year available for hire in that field and the proposed department would duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in one of our existing departments. The proposed Area Studies Department will duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in our existing Anthropology Department. However, we will fund the new department.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following statements follows logically from the university administrator's statements?\n# Options:\nA) If the proposed area studies department did not duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in anthropology, then the new department would not be funded.\nB) The proposed area studies department would not duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in any existing department other than anthropology.\nC) The field of area studies has fewer than 50 people per year available for hire.\nD) The field of area studies has at least 50 people per year available for hire.", "<think>.\nTo determine which statement follows logically from the university administrator's statements, let's break down the given information and analyze each option step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis**:.\n   - The university administrator will not fund a new department if:.\n     - There are fewer than 50 people per year available for hire in that field.\n     - The proposed department would duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in one of our existing departments.\n\n2.**Proposed Area Studies Department**:.\n   - The proposed Area Studies Department will duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in the existing Anthropology Department.\n\n3.**Funding Decision**:.\n   - The university administrator will fund the new department despite the duplication.\n\nNow, let's evaluate each option:.\n\nA) If the proposed area studies department did not duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in anthropology, then the new department would not be funded.\n   - This statement is not necessarily true because the administrator will fund the new department even if it duplicates less than 25 percent of the material covered in anthropology.The field of area studies has more than 50 people per year available for hire, given that the administrator will fund the new department despite the availability of fewer than 50 people per year.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
