large trucks.\nThis option states that even if Partoria makes changes to the regulation of trucking, it will still have to keep some smaller roads off-limits to all large trucks.This does not directly weaken the argument about the accident rate of triple-trailer trucks.\n\nC) Partorian trucking companies have so far used triple-trailer trucks on lightly traveled sections of major highways only.\nThis option suggests that Partorian trucking companies have not yet used triple-trailer trucks on heavily traveled sections of major highways.This does not directly weaken the argument about the accident rate of triple-trailer trucks.\nThe safety record of the trucking industry in Partoria has worsened significantly over the past decade, which directly undermines the argument about the accident rate of triple-trailer trucks.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
