cian.However, this argument is flawed because it assumes that the frequency of haircuts is directly related to the amount of business generated, which is not necessarily true.\n\nB) This option argues that borrowing small amounts of money is not advisable because the interest accumulates over time, leading to a larger debt.This argument is flawed because it assumes that the interest rate is fixed and does not consider the possibility of paying off the debt early or negotiating a lower interest rate.\n\nC) This option suggests that the committee should endorse a plan to postpone construction of the new expressway because many residents of the affected neighborhoods are opposed to it.This argument is flawed because it assumes that the residents' opposition is the only factor to consider, ignoring other potential benefits of the expressway.The argument suggesting that documents of local heritage should not be preserved or archived for future generations is flawed because it fails to consider the value of historical records.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
