cs of another substance (saccharin).\n\nC) After taking sodium chloride and quinine at the same time, drinking water will have a slightly sweet feeling.\nThis option describes a situation where the presence of sodium chloride (a salty substance) and quinine (a bitter substance) together results in a slightly sweet taste when drinking water.This is an example of synergy because the presence of one substance (sodium chloride) enhances the taste characteristics of another substance (quinine).\n\nB) After eating sour sambal, and then eating sour food, you will taste the sour taste.\nThis option describes a situation where the presence of sour sambal (a sour substance) affects the taste of sour food. This is an example of synergy because the presence of one substance (sour sambal) enhances the taste characteristics of another substance (sour food).\n\nBased on the analysis, option B exhibits synergy.\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
